{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Remove a stale backup directory carried in the tickets tree at HEAD. Immediate working-tree win,\nno history rewrite, and a prerequisite for the reclaim. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\nConfirmed present at HEAD: `.bridge_state.bak-retarget/prev_snapshot.json` **33,025,572 bytes** +\n`bindings.json` **15,186 bytes**, from a single static revision (`b3475f0e`, 2026-07-08). It is\nmaterialized by **every worktree checkout** and walked by every GHA `git add -A`.\n\nIt contributes ~0 MB/day, so it does not explain the ongoing growth — this is a one-off 33 MB of dead\nweight. It must land **before** epic 0303-692c's reclaim: the strip removes the directory from\nhistory, and the reclaim's re-add commit restores only the live `.bridge_state` files, so the\ntree-identity assertion depends on this already being gone.\n\nNote the tickets `.gitattributes` glob is `.bridge_state/*`, which does **not** match\n`.bridge_state.bak-retarget/*` — so no merge-driver consideration applies.\n\n## Plan-defect correction during execution\nThe original third criterion said `rebar fsck` must be absolutely clean. The live store already had\n561 diagnostics before this deletion, including intentional permanent `STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED` audit\nevidence that fsck and its integration tests are designed to surface. Absolute zero would require\ndeleting audit history or changing unrelated fsck semantics. The scoped proof that this deletion did\nnot corrupt the store is an unchanged before/after diagnostic multiset plus a green read-only\nreconciler pass. This correction was made only after the completion verifier rejected the literal\nwording; the rejection and exact counts remain recorded in comments and session log dc9a-ea86-ecba-40a0.\n\nExecution-phase plan review also found a now-dead exact-name entry and scrub comment in the live-Jira\nstore-copy fixture. Remove those two references so the repository no longer carries current-store\nlogic for a path deleted from tickets HEAD. This is a test-harness cleanup only; the glob scrub still\nremoves every `.bridge_state*` sibling and preserves fixture isolation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.bridge_state.bak-retarget` is absent from `git ls-tree -r HEAD` on the tickets branch. Tier:\n      **repo assertion**.\n- [ ] Working-tree size of a fresh checkout drops by **>=33 MB**. Tier: **repo measurement**.\n- [ ] `rebar fsck` reports the identical diagnostic multiset before and after deletion (zero new\n      diagnostics), and a read-only reconciler pass completes green afterwards, proving nothing read\n      the backup. Tier: **CLI subprocess** with before/after count-by-kind comparison.\n- [ ] `grep -rn 'bak-retarget' src/ .github/` returns no production consumer. Tier: grep assertion.\n- [ ] The live-Jira store-copy fixture no longer hard-codes the deleted backup name; its `.bridge_state*`\n      glob scrub and store-copy isolation tests remain intact. Tier: **test-harness unit/static check**.\n\n## Files\nTickets-branch `.bridge_state.bak-retarget/`;\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py`.\n\nRollback: revert tickets commit f2837f0a8 to restore the two files, and revert the paired Gerrit test\ncleanup commit. No history rewrite or force push is required.\n\nScope: XS. No dependencies."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785605504121664001,"uuid":"ee93d219-5795-4653-87fb-586efa0d1a1e"}